jt-pve-storage-purestorage (1.1.30-1) stable; urgency=medium

  * Request a filesystem freeze around container snapshots. PVE cgroup-freezes
    an LXC container's processes before calling volume_snapshot(), but only
    freezes the filesystem for storages that ask for it via
    volume_snapshot_needs_fsfreeze(). Without it, dirty pages held by the host
    kernel were not on the array when the array took its snapshot, making
    running-container snapshots -- including vzdump backups in snapshot mode --
    crash-consistent rather than filesystem-consistent. RBD and other
    remote-snapshot storages do the same. QEMU guests are unaffected: their
    quiescing runs through the guest agent.
  * Flush host buffers before a snapshot even when the device is in use. The
    previous guard skipped the flush precisely when a container was running on
    the device, which is the case that has dirty pages to flush.
  * Refuse rename_snapshot() and volume_snapshot_info() explicitly instead of
    inheriting base implementations that route through filesystem_path(),
    which this plugin cannot implement.

 -- Jason Cheng <jason@jason.tools>  Thu, 06 Aug 2026 19:22:20 +0800
